- @pres25_meet_candidates: Meet the candidates one by one

@pres25_meet_candidates
title: [? if pres_2025_united_left: Twelve candidates, eight electoral fields?][? if not pres_2025_united_left: Thirteen candidates, nine electoral fields?]

Only two candidates will survive the first ballot. Our nominee begins outside
those places, but the first round still decides what the Left is worth: whether
its electorate can be found again, whether its issues survive into the runoff,
and what either finalist must offer to borrow its voters for a fortnight.

Before the campaign board opens, we should look at each field the campaign will
be competing against.

- @pres25_meet_trzaskowski: First, the democratic camp's candidate
- @pres25_meet_sikorski: First, the democratic camp's candidate
- @pres25_meet_nowacka: First, the democratic camp's candidate

@pres25_meet_trzaskowski
title: Rafał Trzaskowski — the democratic camp's candidate
view-if: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski-2025.webp

**Rafał Trzaskowski — Civic Coalition**

He carries KO's liberal and local-government electorate, the mayors, the
metropolitan professionals and the voters who treat any anti-PiS ballot as the
only serious use of an election. [? if pres_2025_incumbent: As President, he
must defend five years of signatures, vetoes and cohabitation as well as his
campaign programme.?][? if not pres_2025_incumbent: As Warsaw mayor and the
2020 runner-up, he offers the democratic camp a route from city hall to the
Palace.?]

His weakness is the same as his strength: the camp that must finish the change
of government is also the camp that has been in office long enough to be asked
what it finished.

- @pres25_meet_nawrocki: The right has found a new face
- @pres25_meet_morawiecki: The right has returned to its former prime minister
- @pres25_meet_czarnek: The right has chosen the culture warrior
- @pres25_meet_bochenski: The right has chosen the young manager

@pres25_meet_sikorski
title: Radosław Sikorski — security before the social agenda
view-if: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Radosław Sikorski"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-sikorski.webp

**Radosław Sikorski — foreign minister and Civic Coalition Atlanticist**

Sikorski holds the pro-European security constituency: voters who want NATO,
Washington and a President able to speak the language of allied power without
translation. His campaign is for a Palace that treats deterrence, diplomacy
and the eastern border as the organising work of the office.

He has little interest in making the social agenda part of that work. Labour,
housing and reproductive rights return to Parliament as matters for somebody
else, which gives Lewica a clear argument and leaves KO's progressive voters
wondering what, beyond security, this presidency is for.

- @pres25_meet_nawrocki: The right has found a new face
- @pres25_meet_morawiecki: The right has returned to its former prime minister
- @pres25_meet_czarnek: The right has chosen the culture warrior
- @pres25_meet_bochenski: The right has chosen the young manager

@pres25_meet_nowacka
title: Barbara Nowacka — rights and the secular school
view-if: pres_2025_ko_candidate = "Barbara Nowacka"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-nowacka.webp

**Barbara Nowacka — education minister and Civic Coalition progressive**

Nowacka holds the secular, feminist part of the democratic electorate. Her
campaign is for schools free of clerical direction and a presidential pen
committed to reproductive rights, equal citizenship and the legislation that
the coalition has postponed.

That programme competes directly for our voters, organisers and movement
partners. Its vulnerability is ownership: every undelivered rights promise is
also part of the government's record, and a KO candidacy can absorb Lewica's
language while leaving Lewica to answer for the compromises.

- @pres25_meet_nawrocki: The right has found a new face
- @pres25_meet_morawiecki: The right has returned to its former prime minister
- @pres25_meet_czarnek: The right has chosen the culture warrior
- @pres25_meet_bochenski: The right has chosen the young manager

@pres25_meet_nawrocki
title: Karol Nawrocki — the borrowed civic committee
view-if: pres_2025_right_candidate = "Karol Nawrocki"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-nawrocki.webp

**Karol Nawrocki — historian, president of the Institute of National
Remembrance, backed by PiS**

Nawrocki runs through a formally civic committee with the whole PiS
organisation behind it. The arrangement lets the right exchange a damaged party
brand for a new face without surrendering a single position on the courts, the
church or the shape of the state.

Everything therefore depends on whether voters read the committee as
independence or as a costume. He begins with the largest disciplined electorate
in the field and the least freedom to define himself against the people who
built it.

- @pres25_meet_mentzen: Konfederacja has a leader and a defector
- @pres25_meet_bosak: Konfederacja has a candidate and a defector

@pres25_meet_morawiecki
title: Mateusz Morawiecki — the whole record returns to the ballot
view-if: pres_2025_right_candidate = "Mateusz Morawiecki"
face-image: img/poland/cards/advisor-morawiecki.webp

**Mateusz Morawiecki — PiS's former prime minister**

Morawiecki holds the part of the PiS electorate that wants an active state,
family transfers and a right able to administer more than grievance. The
party's own former prime minister runs for a Palace credible on state capacity,
economic intervention and the social programmes his governments built.

He also carries the whole record: judicial conflict, pandemic procurement,
inflation, European isolation and every promise financed or deferred from the
premiership. There is no civic costume between the candidate and eight years
of government, and no failure he can assign to an unfamiliar predecessor.

- @pres25_meet_mentzen: Konfederacja has a leader and a defector
- @pres25_meet_bosak: Konfederacja has a candidate and a defector

@pres25_meet_czarnek
title: Przemysław Czarnek — the parish campaign
view-if: pres_2025_right_candidate = "Przemysław Czarnek"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-czarnek.webp

**Przemysław Czarnek — former education minister and PiS culture warrior**

Czarnek holds the parish networks, the parents' committees organised against
liberal schooling and the voters who want the presidency to defend a Catholic
nation rather than arbitrate among citizens. His campaign is for permanent
cultural mobilisation from the Palace.

The same record that fills church halls empties almost every room beyond them.
Teachers, younger women, cities and moderate conservatives know his education
ministry already; he can mobilise the right at full volume and repel everyone
else before a second-round appeal begins.

- @pres25_meet_mentzen: Konfederacja has a leader and a defector
- @pres25_meet_bosak: Konfederacja has a candidate and a defector

@pres25_meet_bochenski
title: Tobiasz Bocheński — PiS with the edges filed off
view-if: pres_2025_right_candidate = "Tobiasz Bocheński"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bochenski.webp

**Tobiasz Bocheński — former voivode and Warsaw-facing PiS manager**

Bocheński holds younger administrators, metropolitan conservatives and PiS
voters who want the state run competently without another daily culture war.
His campaign is for a managerial Palace: disciplined, technically fluent and
able to meet Warsaw on its own ground.

He is PiS with the edges filed off, which creates the vulnerability as well as
the opening. The party machine, court record and veto programme remain behind
him; loyalists may find the polish bloodless, while swing voters can still ask
whether a smoother manager changes anything he would sign.

- @pres25_meet_mentzen: Konfederacja has a leader and a defector
- @pres25_meet_bosak: Konfederacja has a candidate and a defector

@pres25_meet_mentzen
title: Sławomir Mentzen — the cheap state on the ballot
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-mentzen-2025.webp
view-if: pres_2025_konf_candidate = "Sławomir Mentzen"

**Sławomir Mentzen — Konfederacja chair, tax adviser**

Mentzen combines market radicalism with nationalist social politics and sells
both as ordinary common sense to men under forty. He competes with **[+
pres_2025_right_surname +]** for
the young right and with everyone for the voters who believe the existing
parties are a cost rather than a choice.

He is also the candidate whose programme can be priced. Every promise he makes
about taxes is a promise about a hospital, a school or a pension that somebody
else will have to close.

- @pres25_meet_braun: The Crown runs separately

@pres25_meet_bosak
title: Krzysztof Bosak — the national movement's disciplined face
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bosak.webp
view-if: pres_2025_konf_candidate = "Krzysztof Bosak"

**Krzysztof Bosak — Sejm deputy and National Movement leader**

Bosak holds Konfederacja's national-conservative constituency: the organised
national movement, younger Catholic conservatives and voters who want a harder
state on borders, family and sovereignty without Braun's permanent spectacle.
His campaign is for a disciplined nationalist Palace rather than Mentzen's
cheap-state insurgency.

That discipline also narrows him. PiS competes for the same patriotic voter,
Braun can always accuse him of moderation, and the campaign lacks Mentzen's
anti-tax digital audience. He can consolidate a movement more easily than he
can explain what lies beyond it.

- @pres25_meet_braun: The Crown runs separately

@pres25_meet_braun
title: Grzegorz Braun — the campaign that wants the scandal
face-image: img/poland/events/grzegorz-braun-2025.webp

**Grzegorz Braun — MEP, leader of the Crown**

Braun has left Konfederacja's common discipline for a personal campaign built
out of confrontation, antisemitic provocation and the certainty that no
broadcaster can ignore him. His candidacy is a bid to prove that Konfederacja
has become another managed party.

[+ pres_2025_konf_surname +] needs Braun's voters without becoming answerable for his conduct. That
gap between the two campaigns is the only part of the radical-right vote any
other candidate can work on.

- @pres25_meet_holownia: Two campaigns claim the space outside the blocs
- @pres25_meet_petru: Two campaigns claim the space outside the blocs

@pres25_meet_holownia
title: Szymon Hołownia — the outsider who returned
view-if: pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Szymon Hołownia"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia-2025.webp

**Szymon Hołownia — founder and leader of Poland 2050**

[? if p2050_2023_exclusion_comeback_done: Hołownia enters the race after
refounding his movement against both PiS and KO. The campaign is no longer an
appeal to remember 2020: Poland 2050 has taken support from Konfederacja,
absorbed Zieloni and proved that it can survive outside the two dominant
blocs. He begins as a serious third contender for the runoff.?]
[? if not p2050_2023_exclusion_comeback_done:
Hołownia can no longer run as a man untouched by parliamentary power. He offers
institutional reform and a centrist escape from the leading pair while
defending what his movement did with its share of government, which is a harder
speech than the one he gave in 2020.?]

His voters are the most genuinely undecided electorate on the ballot, and in a
runoff they will be the most expensive to buy.

- @pres25_meet_stanowski: And the campaign about campaigns

@pres25_meet_petru
title: Ryszard Petru — the centre prices the state
view-if: pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Ryszard Petru"
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-petru.webp

**Ryszard Petru — Poland 2050's market-liberal economist**

Petru holds the market-liberal wing of Poland 2050: entrepreneurs, urban
professionals and centrist voters who want every promise accompanied by a
cost. His campaign is for a presidency that audits legislation, restrains
spending and treats economic credibility as the first institutional reform.

He prices everything, including the public services and transfers his party's
less liberal voters depend on. That makes him legible and vulnerable at once:
Lewica can answer every veto threat with the ward, school or household that
would pay for it, while Hołownia's personal electorate may simply stay home.

- @pres25_meet_stanowski: And the campaign about campaigns

@pres25_meet_stanowski
title: Krzysztof Stanowski — the candidacy as commentary
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-stanowski.webp

**Krzysztof Stanowski — media entrepreneur, founder of Kanał Zero**

Stanowski campaigns partly as an investigation of campaign ritual itself: he
files his spending, mocks the format and interviews his rivals in it. His
audience gives him reach that no party office can match and no party
organisation can convert.

Every studio that treats him as comic relief supplies his critique with another
exhibit. His vote is small; the argument he makes about who gets heard is not.

- @pres25_meet_minor: The five smaller committees

@pres25_meet_minor
title: Five smaller committees, five separate candidacies

Five further candidates complete the ballot.

**Joanna Senyszyn**, a former SLD parliamentarian, offers secular social
democracy outside Lewica's organisation.

**Artur Bartoszewicz**, an economist, runs an expert and anti-party campaign.

**Marek Jakubiak**, a former MP and brewer, offers a national-conservative
business voice.

**Maciej Maciak**, a local broadcaster, and **Marek Woch**, a legal campaigner,
complete the ballot from outside every national organisation.

They share one row only in the simulation. Senyszyn can take disappointed older
Left voters; Jakubiak competes on the nationalist flank; together they can turn
a small combined vote into a much larger argument about whose campaign was
allowed to be heard.

- @pres25_meet_left: Finally, our own nominee

@pres25_meet_left
title: [+ pres_2025_left_candidate +] — our nominee

**[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]** carries the campaign selected through **[+
pres_2025_nomination_method +]**.

[? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat": Biejat joins housing,
care and reproductive freedom to the claim that the Left can use institutions
without disappearing inside them.?][? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Agnieszka
Dziemianowicz-Bąk": Dziemianowicz-Bąk joins labour law, public services and
social security to a record that can be inspected rather than merely
promised.?][? if pres_2025_left_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": Zandberg joins
wages, housing and public investment to a refusal of the liberal economic
limits accepted by every leading camp.?]

<div class="face-figure left-candidate-portrait" data-candidate-quality="pres_2025_left_candidate"><img class="face-img" alt="Portrait of the Left's presidential nominee"></div>

[? if not pres_2025_united_left: <span class="party-razem"><b>Adrian Zandberg</b></span> also appears on the
ballot for Razem. He is a rival candidate with an overlapping electorate—not a
second version of our nominee.?][? if pres_2025_united_left: Razem has no
second candidate. Its organisers are bound to the same nomination, and
Zandberg cannot appear in two campaign rows.?]

- @pres25_opening_poll: Release the opening poll

@calculate_presidential_poll_2025
on-arrival: {!
const finitePoll25 = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
const pollIds25 = [
    "ko", "right", "left", "razem", "mentzen",
    "braun", "holownia", "stanowski", "other"
];
const candidateBase25 =
    Q.pres_2025_left_candidate == "Adrian Zandberg" ? 4.86 :
    (Q.pres_2025_left_candidate == "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk"
        ? 4.55 : 4.23);
const leftIntent25 = finitePoll25(Q.left_vote_intent, 8.61);
const breakthrough25 = Math.max(0, leftIntent25 - 12);
const campaign25 = finitePoll25(Q.pres_2025_campaign_strength, 0);
const debate25 = Q.pres_2025_poll_stage == "tracking"
    ? finitePoll25(Q.pres_2025_debate_bonus, 0)
    : 0;
const leftBase25 = Q.pres_2025_united_left
    ? 7.70 + (candidateBase25 - 4.23) * 0.45 +
        (leftIntent25 - 8.61) * 0.55 + breakthrough25 * 1.30 +
        campaign25 * 0.20 + debate25
    : candidateBase25 +
        (leftIntent25 - 8.61) * 0.28 + breakthrough25 * 1.80 +
        campaign25 * 0.20 + debate25;
const razemBase25 = Q.pres_2025_united_left ? 0 :
    4.86 +
    (finitePoll25(Q.razem_vote_intent, 4.86) - 4.86) * 0.80 +
    (finitePoll25(Q.razem_strength, 20) - 20) * 0.06;
const rawPoll25 = {
    ko: 31.36 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.ko_vote_intent, 30.70) - 30.70) * 0.34 -
        Math.max(0, leftBase25 + razemBase25 - 10) * 0.18,
    right: 29.54 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.pis_vote_intent, 35.38) - 35.38) * 0.25 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.far_right_agenda, 32) - 32) * 0.018,
    left: Math.max(0.4, leftBase25),
    razem: Math.max(0, razemBase25),
    mentzen: (Q.pres_2025_konf_candidate == "Krzysztof Bosak" ? 13.9 : 14.81) +
        (finitePoll25(Q.konf_vote_intent, 7.16) - 7.16) * 0.35 +
        (Q.pres_2025_konf_candidate == "Krzysztof Bosak"
            ? (finitePoll25(Q.konf_nationalist_share, 35) - 35) * 0.03
            : (finitePoll25(Q.konf_mentzenite_share, 47) - 47) * 0.025),
    braun: 6.34 + finitePoll25(Q.braun_martyrdom, 0) * 0.06 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.konf_braunist_share, 18) - 18) * 0.025,
    holownia: 4.99 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.p2050_vote_intent, 4) - 4) * 0.25 +
        finitePoll25(Q.p2050_holownia_presidential_bonus, 0),
    stanowski: 1.24 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.kanal_zero_capacity, 12) - 12) * 0.025 +
        finitePoll25(Q.pres_2025_stanowski_surge, 0),
    other: 2.63
};
if (Q.pres_2025_incumbent) {
    rawPoll25.ko += 1.2 +
        (finitePoll25(Q.public_trust, 43) - 43) * 0.035 +
        finitePoll25(Q.trz_vetoes, 0) * 0.10;
}
if (Q.pres_2025_poll_stage == "tracking") {
    for (const id of pollIds25) {
        if (id == "other") continue;
        rawPoll25[id] += finitePoll25(Q["pres_2025_rival_shift_" + id], 0);
    }
}
const noisePrefix25 = Q.pres_2025_poll_stage == "opening"
    ? "pres_2025_open_noise_" : "pres_2025_track_noise_";
for (const id of pollIds25) {
    if (id == "razem" && Q.pres_2025_united_left) {
        rawPoll25[id] = 0;
    } else {
        rawPoll25[id] = Math.max(
            id == "other" ? 0.3 : 0.1,
            rawPoll25[id] + finitePoll25(Q[noisePrefix25 + id], 0)
        );
    }
}
const pollTotal25 = pollIds25.reduce(function(sum, id) {
    return sum + rawPoll25[id];
}, 0);
const displayPoll25 = {};
for (const id of pollIds25) {
    displayPoll25[id] = Math.round(
        rawPoll25[id] * 1000 / Math.max(1, pollTotal25)
    ) / 10;
}
const roundedTotal25 = pollIds25.reduce(function(sum, id) {
    return sum + displayPoll25[id];
}, 0);
displayPoll25.other = Math.round(
    (displayPoll25.other + 100 - roundedTotal25) * 10
) / 10;
for (const id of pollIds25) {
    Q["pres_2025_poll_" + id] = displayPoll25[id];
}
Q.stanowski_best_poll = Math.max(
    finitePoll25(Q.stanowski_best_poll, 1.24),
    finitePoll25(Q.pres_2025_poll_stanowski, 0)
);
Q.stanowski_trigger_score = Math.max(
    finitePoll25(Q.stanowski_trigger_score, 0),
    finitePoll25(Q.pres_2025_poll_stanowski, 0)
);
if (Q.pres_2025_poll_stage == "tracking") {
    Q.pres_2025_debate_shift = Math.round(
        (displayPoll25.left -
            finitePoll25(Q.pres_2025_debate_poll_before_left, 0)) * 10
    ) / 10;
}
!}

@pres25_opening_poll
title: The opening presidential poll
new-page: true
on-arrival: pres_2025_poll_stage = "opening"
call: calculate_presidential_poll_2025

= A national race with a ±2.2 point working margin

The estimate uses current party support, candidate strength, organisation and
the nomination settlement. The five smallest committees remain aggregated;
their candidates remain separate on the real ballot.

<div class="poll-table">
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-ko"><b>[+ pres_2025_ko_candidate +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_ko +]%</span><span>KO</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-pis"><b>[+ pres_2025_right_surname +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_right +]%</span><span>PiS-backed</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-konf"><b>[+ pres_2025_konf_surname +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_mentzen +]%</span><span>Konf.</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-konf"><b>Braun</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_braun +]%</span><span>Korona</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-p2050"><b>[+ pres_2025_centre_surname +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_holownia +]%</span><span>PL2050</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>Stanowski</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_stanowski +]%</span><span>independent</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-lewica"><b>[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_left +]%</span><span>Lewica</span></div>
[? if not pres_2025_united_left: <div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-razem"><b>Zandberg</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_razem +]%</span><span>Razem</span></div>?]
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>Five smaller committees</b></span><span>[+ pres_2025_poll_other +]%</span><span>combined estimate</span></div>
</div>

- @pres25_campaign_menu: Open the two-move campaign board

@pres25_campaign_menu
title: Two decisions before the national debates
new-page: true

= Campaign board — [+ pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining +] moves remain

Every operation can be used once. The poll describes the present; the campaign
decides which electorate the nominee will try to change.

- @pres25_campaign_work
- @pres25_campaign_rights
- @pres25_campaign_counties
- @pres25_campaign_constitution
- @pres25_campaign_left_ground

@pres25_campaign_work
title: Put wages, housing and public services on one tour
subtitle: Free. Strong material ownership; less room for democratic-camp positioning.
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_work = 0
on-arrival: pres_2025_campaign_work = 1; pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 3; labor_credibility += 3; workers_support += 2; household_security += 1; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 9; public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 8; news_headline = "The presidential campaign becomes a test of wages, homes and services"

The tour drops the constitutional vocabulary and runs on rent statements, ward
closures and pay slips. It is the cheapest operation on the board because the
material is already ours: every union branch and tenants' committee the party
has ever worked with can host it without a fee.

The cost is positional. KO's people complain that the Left is campaigning
against the government rather than against **[+ pres_2025_right_surname +]**,
and the studios ask, more
than once, whether **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]** understands what this
election is actually about.

- @pres25_campaign_next
- @pres25_campaign_done

@pres25_campaign_rights
title: Join equality organisations to the national tour
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Mobilises women and younger voters; deepens the break with PSL.
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_rights = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign cannot finance the legal and organiser network.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_rights = 1; pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 2.5; progressive_credibility += 3; feminist_trust += 4; women_support += 2; psl_relation -= 3; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 10; public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += 8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 7; news_headline = "Equality organisations enter the presidential ground campaign"

The abortion-rights networks, the legal clinics and the student organisations
bring their own lists, their own lawyers and an audience that has spent two
years being told the promise would come later. They do not campaign for us out
of loyalty; they campaign because the presidential signature is the exact
obstacle they keep meeting.

PSL's county chairs read the same footage and conclude that the Left has chosen
its side of the coalition argument in public. They are not wrong, and they will
remember it in the runoff bargaining.

- @pres25_campaign_next
- @pres25_campaign_done

@pres25_campaign_counties
title: Build a county tour beyond the metropolitan Left
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Slower media rhythm; durable local and rural reach.
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_counties = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign cannot finance the county route.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_counties = 1; pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 2.2; local_network += 4; rural_support += 3; psl_relation += 1; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "The nominee leaves the studio circuit for the county map"

Two buses, forty towns, a bus timetable that no longer serves half of them.
**[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]** spends the month in places where Lewica has
never had a functioning branch and where the argument about hospital wards and
rail connections needs no translation.

National coverage suffers: a county market at nine in the morning does not make
the evening bulletin. What it makes instead is a list of names in districts
that had none, and the campaign will still have that list after the count.

- @pres25_campaign_next
- @pres25_campaign_done

@pres25_campaign_constitution
title: Publish a lawful-presidency and veto standard
subtitle: Free. Builds governing credibility; makes the current Palace and KO answer the same test.
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_constitution = 0
on-arrival: pres_2025_campaign_constitution = 1; pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 1.8; constitutional_restraint += 3; judicial_repair_mandate += 2; public_trust += 2; president_relation -= 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 9; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 8; news_headline = "The Left publishes one constitutional standard for every president"

The document is short and deliberately unflattering to everyone: what a
president may refuse to sign, what a president may not refuse to do, and which
appointments must be published before they are made. It commits our own nominee
first, which is the only reason anyone else has to answer it.

The Palace treats the publication as an attack, because it is one applied
evenly. KO's lawyers find nothing in it they can disown, and start quoting the
parts that embarrass the other camp.

- @pres25_campaign_next
- @pres25_campaign_done

@pres25_campaign_left_ground
title: [? if pres_2025_united_left: Put every Left organisation behind one field operation?][? if not pres_2025_united_left: Negotiate a no-fratricide ground pact with Razem?]
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Protects Left turnout; blurs the line between rival programmes.
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_left_ground = 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Parallel organiser networks cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_2025_campaign_left_ground = 1; pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_2025_campaign_strength += 3.5; razem_cooperation += 5; party_unity += 2; local_network += 2; news_headline = "The Left protects its shared ground before the presidential count"

[? if pres_2025_united_left: Every current that lost the nomination is given
something to run: a region, a constituency, a phone bank of its own. Nobody is
asked to pretend the argument is settled, only to keep it inside the same
campaign until the ballots are counted.?][? if not pres_2025_united_left: The
two headquarters sign a short list of things neither campaign will do to the
other: no attack material, no poaching of local organisers, no briefing against
the other's candidate in the last fortnight. Zandberg's people insist the pact
be published, so that breaking it costs something.?]

The operation is expensive and its benefit is invisible until the count: a Left
electorate that stays a Left electorate instead of leaking to KO out of anxiety
or to the sofa out of boredom.

- @pres25_campaign_next
- @pres25_campaign_done

@pres25_campaign_next
title: Return to the campaign board
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining > 0
go-to: pres25_campaign_menu

@pres25_campaign_done
title: Close the campaign board and let the month run
view-if: pres_2025_campaign_actions_remaining <= 0
go-to: poland_event_queue

@braun_breaks_konf
# scenario-ledger: FAR-02
# prose-audit: Grade B — Braun and Mentzen are introduced as rival radical-right organisers with different constituencies, and each Lewica response now changes the public meaning of the split on screen.
title: Braun's place inside Konfederacja is decided
subtitle: Organisational strength determines whether the federation disciplines him, bargains or breaks
face-image: img/poland/events/grzegorz-braun-2025.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 25
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.braun_legal_preparation = Number(Q.braun_legal_preparation) || 0;
const kkpRecord = (Q.rival_group_records || []).find(function(record) {
    return record && record.id == "kkp";
});
const braunistOrganisation = Math.max(
    Number(Q.konf_braunist_share) || 0,
    kkpRecord ? Number(kkpRecord.organisation) || 0 : 0
);
const braunStays = braunistOrganisation >= 55 &&
    Number(Q.far_right_fragmentation || 0) < 35;
if (braunStays) {
    Q.far_right_split = 0;
    Q.braun_federation_outcome = braunistOrganisation >= 68
        ? "Konfederacja accepts Braun's presidential candidacy"
        : "Konfederacja buys Braun's withdrawal with protected list places";
    if (braunistOrganisation >= 68) {
        Q.pres_2025_konf_candidate = "Grzegorz Braun";
    }
    Q.konf_braunist_share += 3;
    Q.far_right_fragmentation += 2;
    if (Q.trz_freebie_law) {
        Q.konf_normalisation -= 3;
        Q.far_right_agenda += 3;
        Q.minority_safety -= 2;
    }
Q.public_mood_pending_secular_state_salience += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 5;
    Q.news_headline = Q.braun_federation_outcome;
} else {
    Q.far_right_split = 1;
    Q.braun_federation_outcome =
        "Braun leaves Konfederacja with Korona as an independent vehicle";
    if (Q.konf_seats >= 1) {
        Q.korona_seats += 1;
        Q.konf_seats -= 1;
    }
    if (kkpRecord) {
        kkpRecord.active = 1;
        kkpRecord.contesting = 1;
        kkpRecord.list_committee = "kkp";
        kkpRecord.exclusive_seats = Math.max(1, kkpRecord.exclusive_seats || 0);
    }
    Q.konf_braunist_share -= 8;
    Q.konf_mentzenite_share += 5;
    Q.konf_nationalist_share += 3;
    if (Q.trz_freebie_law) {
        Q.konf_normalisation += 5;
        Q.far_right_fragmentation += 5;
    }
    Q.news_headline =
        "Braun takes a seat and an electoral vehicle out of Konfederacja";
}
!}

= January 2025 — Two radical-right electorates

Far-right MEP <span class="party-korona"><b>Grzegorz Braun</b></span> challenges
New Hope leader <span class="party-konf"><b>Sławomir Mentzen</b></span> for the
federation's presidential nomination. Mentzen wants younger anti-tax voters
and coalition respectability; Braun wants a personal movement unrestrained by
the federation's discipline.

**[+ braun_federation_outcome +].** [? if far_right_split: Any elected
representation declared for Braun moves with his organisation; no undeclared
MP is reassigned.?][? if not far_right_split: Crown keeps its organisation
inside the federation. Protected places or a nomination settle this congress,
but do not erase the rivalry.?]

Jewish organisations, minority advocates and people targeted by Braun's public
actions need protection. Lewica also has to understand that calling every
Konfederacja voter a Braun supporter can hand Mentzen the respectable image he
could not earn alone. The split presents two threats, not one convenient label.

- @braun_isolate
- @braun_attack_all
- @braun_watch

@braun_isolate
title: Treat Braun and Mentzen as distinct threats
subtitle: Deny Braun a common persecution story, while Mentzen tries to pass for the responsible successor.
on-arrival: public_trust += 2; media_capacity += 2; braun_martyrdom -= 2; braun_legal_preparation += 1; konf_relation += 1; far_right_agenda -= 1; news_headline = "The Left refuses to reunite the radical right rhetorically"

Lewica's briefings name Braun's Crown movement and Mentzen's Konfederacja
separately, then document what each one says and organises. Mentzen receives no
absolution for expelling a rival; Braun loses the larger federation he needs
for a ready-made persecution story.

- @poland_event_queue: File the two-threat briefing

@braun_attack_all
title: Make every Konfederacja figure answer for Braun
subtitle: Satisfy anti-fascist organisers, at the risk of giving both successor camps the contrast they want.
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 3; konf_mentzenite_share += 3; braun_martyrdom += 3; braun_legal_preparation -= 1 if braun_legal_preparation >= 1; far_right_agenda += 2; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "Mentzen uses Braun's expulsion to advertise respectability"

Every camera appearance treats Braun as proof of what Konfederacja always was.
The line satisfies anti-fascist organisers, but Mentzen answers with the image
of the man who imposed discipline while Braun tells supporters that the whole
system fears him. Both successor campaigns find a use for our simplification.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the unified attack

@braun_watch
title: Build a legal and media watch around both successor camps
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Monitoring capacity is already committed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; media_capacity += 3; minority_safety += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 1; braun_martyrdom -= 1; braun_legal_preparation += 4; news_headline = "Two far-right organisations receive one evidence archive"

Party lawyers, minority organisations and local monitors build one archive
with two clearly marked files. Threats can reach potential victims before they
become clips, and later prosecutors will not need a campaign slogan to tell one
organisation's conduct from the other's.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the archive to the events desk
